WEBVTT

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:21.410
Wait!

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:23.500
You're it!

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:39.910
<i>In this world,</i>
<i>there's an invisible magic circle.</i>

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.330
You're it!

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:46.410
What are you doing?

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:50.370
-So you did date him!
-What?

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:56.370
<i>There's an inside and an outside.</i>

00:00:57.870 --> 00:00:59.790
Capture the movement.

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:01.580
-It's hard.
-Right?

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:04.700
-Let's see.
-Hey, not yet!

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:06.830
<i>These people are inside the circle.</i>

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:12.540
<i>And I'm outside.</i>

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.910
<i>But I don't really care.</i>

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:18.540
How's it coming?

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:25.660
Um, I... kind of messed up.

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:27.910
Let me have a look.

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:41.540
Oh, no. Are you okay?

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:43.290
Hey, hey...

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:54.120
<i>I...</i>

00:01:57.290 --> 00:01:58.660
<i>I hate myself.</i>

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:19.500
Anna...

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:22.910
You're fine now.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:26.580
Oh, I'm so glad. Thank you, Doctor.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:31.160
Anna, do you feel all right now?

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:32.160
I'm fine.

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:35.660
You looked like you were in agony.

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:37.660
Where was your inhaler?

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:41.660
I cost you money again.

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:44.040
Why do you say that?

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:48.910
Oh, Miyoko.

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:53.290
I brought Anna's bag.
Her notebook is inside.

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:55.080
Why, thank you.

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:58.330
We were just nearby.
If there's anything else...

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:00.290
Wait...

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:04.160
Has Anna been getting along with you?

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.500
She tells me nothing about school.

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:08.500
She's okay.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.500
But she's very quiet.

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:13.000
Quiet? More like...

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:14.660
Hey, don't.

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:17.540
We're just a bit loud.

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:21.540
Well, take care.

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:25.120
Ever the worrywart, your mother.

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:30.080
Mother...

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:36.370
She's probably a loner at school.

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:40.870
It's true that stress
can trigger asthma attacks.

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:44.000
Meanwhile,
my husband's off on a business trip.

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:48.750
Maybe he and I are partly to blame, too.

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:51.000
12 years old...

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:53.410
It's a difficult age.

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:57.160
Have you noticed anything about her?

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:02.410
She... always has a straight face.

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:04.250
A straight face?

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:08.500
I'm sorry.

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:14.290
Like she won't show her emotions...

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:17.410
She used to be more expressive.

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:22.000
But these days, I don't even know...

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:29.540
Maybe it's because we're not related
by blood.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:35.370
You may want to send her
somewhere to get better.

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:44.160
7:03 DEPARTURE FOR KUSHIRO

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:51.160
<i>Say, Anna...</i>

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:56.160
<i>Do you remember Uncle and Aunt Oiwa?</i>

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:01.160
<i>The air is very clean where they live.</i>

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:09.200
<i>It'll help your condition</i>
<i>to spend some time there.</i>

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:15.290
<i>I can't go with you,</i>
<i>but they'll take care of you.</i>

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:19.620
<i>Be a good girl, eat well,</i>

00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:21.700
<i>and come back nice and happy.</i>

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.540
<i>She whines like a goat.</i>

00:06:13.910 --> 00:06:16.040
Oh, here she is.

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:18.290
Anna.

00:06:23.410 --> 00:06:24.580
Remember us?

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:27.620
No, but Auntie told me all about you.

00:06:28.370 --> 00:06:29.450
I'm Anna Sasaki.

00:06:29.540 --> 00:06:32.870
I hope I'm not much trouble.
Thank you for having me.

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:36.250
Our pleasure.

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:37.870
Auntie?

00:06:38.450 --> 00:06:39.790
She means Yoriko.

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:46.870
Hop on in. Sorry it's a bit of a clunker.

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:57.290
Sorry. It's a bit cramped in here.

00:06:57.370 --> 00:06:58.660
I don't mind at all.

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:04.660
This area's changed since I was last here.
All these new shops.

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:08.540
Where we're headed
is a nice, relaxing place.

00:07:09.330 --> 00:07:13.330
But since the highway was built,
people stopped coming.

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:33.500
They still haven't fixed that pothole!

00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:38.450
I hear you have asthma?

00:07:38.540 --> 00:07:39.750
Uh, yes...

00:07:39.830 --> 00:07:42.450
The air here will fix you up in no time.

00:07:50.830 --> 00:07:54.620
Nice place, huh?
Bet you'd like Auntie to see it, too.

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:56.160
What's that over there?

00:07:57.540 --> 00:07:58.620
On the cliff.

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:03.370
Oh, that's a silo.
It's for storing feed for livestock.

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:06.580
Hasn't been used in decades, though.

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:10.330
Now the village kids use it for dares.

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:13.540
They say there are ghosts there.

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:15.330
Dear, please!

00:08:15.790 --> 00:08:18.290
He loves stories like that.

00:08:18.370 --> 00:08:20.120
Best to stay away from there.

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:27.540
Look, that's our house over there.

00:08:33.620 --> 00:08:36.830
-Do you mind taking this in?
-What's this?

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:40.330
Why would you accept this?

00:08:41.910 --> 00:08:44.290
It's too much for us to eat.

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:48.080
He's always accepting gifts
without thinking...

00:08:50.370 --> 00:08:53.200
Our kids are all grown up and moved out.

00:08:53.660 --> 00:08:55.790
-Make yourself at home.
-Thank you.

00:08:56.330 --> 00:08:58.950
Let's see, where do these go?

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:01.080
Excuse me.

00:09:02.870 --> 00:09:04.080
MOM
DAD

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:13.120
You must think it's an odd house.

00:09:13.750 --> 00:09:15.370
No, it's a lovely home.

00:09:17.580 --> 00:09:19.870
No need for flattery.

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:24.250
Your room's upstairs.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:27.830
It was my daughter's room.

00:09:30.330 --> 00:09:34.750
It'd be sad to clear everything,
so I left it as it was.

00:09:35.500 --> 00:09:36.660
I see.

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:40.250
She's a yoga teacher in Tokyo now.

00:09:40.660 --> 00:09:43.120
I'm thinking of trying it myself.

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:48.120
Oh, and feel free to use
the closet and shelves.

00:09:48.660 --> 00:09:49.790
Oh, thank you.

00:09:58.290 --> 00:10:02.580
"Write and tell me how you are, whatever
you wish to tell me about. Yoriko"

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:06.830
Postcards, how quaint!
You should write her.

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:09.040
Come here for a sec!

00:10:09.370 --> 00:10:10.660
Coming!

00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:13.540
He can be so pushy.

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:15.040
See you later.

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:22.700
Smells like someone else's home.

00:10:56.330 --> 00:10:57.950
Feels nice.

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:00.620
<i>I've arrived safely.</i>

00:11:01.160 --> 00:11:02.830
<i>It's quite nice here.</i>

00:11:03.450 --> 00:11:06.330
<i>Mr. and Mrs. Oiwa are both very kind.</i>

00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:14.330
TO YORIKO SASAKI

00:11:20.870 --> 00:11:22.000
These are delicious.

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:25.370
Sorry, my hands are full.

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:28.000
Um, I'm going to the post office.

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:30.950
Sure, go ahead.

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:32.120
Won't you try this?

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:33.950
Later.

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:36.370
Okay, I'll save it for dessert.

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:48.200
By the way,
there's a shortcut by the parking lot.

00:11:48.290 --> 00:11:49.250
Oh, thank you.

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:51.660
SHORTCUT

00:11:55.330 --> 00:11:57.540
This is the shortcut?

00:11:59.950 --> 00:12:01.660
SHORTCUT

00:12:07.620 --> 00:12:09.080
SHORTCUT

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:18.450
SHORTCUT

00:12:23.660 --> 00:12:26.160
KITAHARA GROCERIES

00:12:30.700 --> 00:12:33.200
Boys just drive me mad!

00:12:33.290 --> 00:12:35.160
It's tough being class president.

00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:37.620
Wait, I need to drop off a letter.

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:46.620
Hey, who's that?

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:16.370
Why is it...

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:21.500
That mansion feels familiar.

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:55.950
I wonder if anyone lives here.

00:14:01.830 --> 00:14:03.700
Excuse me...

00:14:19.370 --> 00:14:21.330
What a big house.

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:55.910
I guess there's no one here.

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:36.500
Oh, no...

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:01.450
I'm sorry.

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:23.750
<i>He's a bear. Or maybe a sea lion.</i>

00:16:52.330 --> 00:16:53.700
Sounds like an adventure!

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:57.580
Completely different in high tide,
isn't it?

00:16:57.660 --> 00:16:59.700
It's the power of the moon.

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:04.080
But imagine that,
Toichi giving a girl a ride on his boat.

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:08.830
He's actually a good guy.
Just not much of a talker.

00:17:11.370 --> 00:17:13.660
You should ask him for a ride again.

00:17:14.540 --> 00:17:16.410
Ask him for a ride.

00:17:18.790 --> 00:17:19.700
I will.

00:17:20.500 --> 00:17:24.750
But it's best you stay away
from the marsh house.

00:17:26.330 --> 00:17:28.160
How come?

00:17:29.750 --> 00:17:31.290
-Ghosts.
-Not again!

00:17:33.370 --> 00:17:34.790
I'll get some wine.

00:17:35.580 --> 00:17:37.660
It looked like no one lives there.

00:17:37.750 --> 00:17:39.450
Not now, anyway.

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:44.160
It used to be a vacation home
for some foreigners.

00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:47.660
Then it changed hands a few times.

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:50.660
But it's been vacant for a while now.

00:17:51.870 --> 00:17:53.450
I see...

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:22.870
Someone's there.

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:07.370
Have you finished them yet?

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:10.700
What Mrs. Kadoya asked for.

00:19:10.790 --> 00:19:12.200
Oh... Almost done.

00:19:12.870 --> 00:19:14.700
Hey, Anna. Going out?

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:16.040
Yes.

00:19:16.540 --> 00:19:18.540
Just finish them already...

00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:22.290
I'm going to go sketch.

00:19:22.370 --> 00:19:23.790
Sure, go on.

00:19:23.870 --> 00:19:24.870
Thank you.

00:19:29.450 --> 00:19:33.870
Yoriko was worried about her,
but she looks fine to me.

00:19:34.790 --> 00:19:37.370
<i>As long as she's having fun</i>
<i>and eating well.</i>

00:19:38.120 --> 00:19:39.370
<i>That's for sure.</i>

00:19:43.750 --> 00:19:47.330
All the trash you pick up
will be collected here.

00:19:47.410 --> 00:19:49.830
Everyone listen!

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:51.250
Now begin!

00:19:54.790 --> 00:19:56.370
Look, it's Toichi.

00:19:56.450 --> 00:19:57.620
Toichi the mute!

00:19:57.700 --> 00:20:01.120
Toichi who only talks once a decade!

00:20:01.450 --> 00:20:04.620
Hey, I said we're not going
there until later!

00:20:04.700 --> 00:20:06.870
We're just checking it out!

00:20:06.950 --> 00:20:08.040
See ya!

00:20:08.120 --> 00:20:11.290
Perhaps we'll hear from you next time!

00:21:12.540 --> 00:21:13.700
I'm going out.

00:21:14.700 --> 00:21:15.870
Wait, Anna.

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:21.540
I have a little errand, so hold on.

00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:25.290
Yes.

00:21:28.450 --> 00:21:30.950
He should be delivering these himself.

00:21:31.040 --> 00:21:33.790
"I'm allergic to that lady," he says!

00:21:34.540 --> 00:21:37.290
But Mrs. Kadoya's been wanting
to meet you.

00:21:38.200 --> 00:21:41.540
Their daughter Nobuko
is a year older than you.

00:21:44.910 --> 00:21:47.290
Nobuko is at cram school today.

00:21:47.910 --> 00:21:49.500
Oh, that's too bad.

00:21:49.580 --> 00:21:52.290
This must be Anna. Nice to meet you.

00:21:54.250 --> 00:21:56.830
Oh, um... Hello.

00:21:56.910 --> 00:21:59.540
Ah, so you draw, I see?

00:22:00.080 --> 00:22:01.450
Show me next time.

00:22:01.540 --> 00:22:03.290
No, I'm not very good.

00:22:03.910 --> 00:22:09.790
Oh, you should go to the Tanabata Festival
with Nobuko tomorrow.

00:22:09.870 --> 00:22:13.910
Great idea! I should still have
my daughter's yukata.

00:22:14.410 --> 00:22:16.660
You can wear it to the festival.

00:22:17.910 --> 00:22:18.750
But...

00:22:20.410 --> 00:22:21.040
Yes.

00:22:21.580 --> 00:22:24.250
I'll let Nobuko know. Now come in.

00:22:25.080 --> 00:22:26.250
Where'd I put it...

00:22:26.330 --> 00:22:28.040
Uh, actually I...

00:22:28.540 --> 00:22:31.290
Oh, you're going sketching. Go ahead!

00:22:34.450 --> 00:22:35.370
She'll look great!

00:22:35.950 --> 00:22:37.870
Ready, and...

00:22:37.950 --> 00:22:39.950
-This one, too.
-Got it.

00:22:40.620 --> 00:22:42.040
I won't look good in it.

00:22:43.790 --> 00:22:45.120
None of her business.

00:22:57.790 --> 00:22:58.950
He's not here.

00:23:26.540 --> 00:23:28.790
-Bye.
-See you tomorrow.

00:23:59.080 --> 00:24:00.830
The tide is out.

00:24:23.370 --> 00:24:24.500
Again.

00:24:34.540 --> 00:24:36.080
I hate festivals.

00:24:44.160 --> 00:24:45.370
Hey, let's go.

00:24:45.450 --> 00:24:46.870
Wait for me.

00:24:47.330 --> 00:24:49.660
-Here you go.
-Thank you.

00:24:49.750 --> 00:24:51.830
-Here's some candy.
-Thanks.

00:24:53.330 --> 00:24:56.750
I wish I was wearing a yukata, too.

00:24:56.830 --> 00:24:58.750
At least you're comfortable.

00:24:58.830 --> 00:25:01.620
Mom forces her tastes on me. It's awful.

00:25:02.120 --> 00:25:03.580
I think it looks cute.

00:25:03.660 --> 00:25:05.370
What? No way!

00:25:06.000 --> 00:25:08.580
It's boring and tacky...

00:25:08.660 --> 00:25:11.330
So Anna, where are you from?

00:25:12.160 --> 00:25:13.200
From Sapporo.

00:25:13.290 --> 00:25:16.950
Cool, I bet the city has great shopping.

00:25:17.040 --> 00:25:20.620
-Maybe lots of cute boys, too?
-You be quiet.

00:25:20.700 --> 00:25:21.700
Sure, sure.

00:25:22.040 --> 00:25:24.700
Here in the boonies.

00:25:25.540 --> 00:25:27.700
Why'd you come out here?

00:25:28.370 --> 00:25:29.790
Well...

00:25:29.870 --> 00:25:32.580
What's this? Nobuko!

00:25:32.660 --> 00:25:33.660
What is it?

00:25:34.870 --> 00:25:38.290
He's always making the same mistakes.

00:25:38.370 --> 00:25:40.370
I'll warn him next time.

00:25:44.370 --> 00:25:46.910
TANABATA FESTIVAL

00:25:47.950 --> 00:25:49.040
There it is.

00:25:49.120 --> 00:25:50.290
Will my wish come true?

00:25:50.370 --> 00:25:53.370
Can I have a candle?

00:25:53.870 --> 00:25:55.000
Here you go.

00:26:04.580 --> 00:26:06.080
Write your wish on this.

00:26:09.080 --> 00:26:10.750
My wish...

00:26:12.540 --> 00:26:14.040
Can you reach?

00:26:14.120 --> 00:26:15.080
Ow!

00:26:15.910 --> 00:26:17.250
Sorry about that.

00:26:20.580 --> 00:26:21.580
Anna!

00:26:21.660 --> 00:26:25.580
Hey, where were you?
I was looking for you.

00:26:26.080 --> 00:26:27.750
Oh, your wish.

00:26:28.910 --> 00:26:29.580
Let's see...

00:26:30.580 --> 00:26:33.580
"I wish for a normal life everyday."

00:26:34.250 --> 00:26:35.660
"Normal"?

00:26:35.750 --> 00:26:38.540
Anna, what do you mean by normal?

00:26:38.620 --> 00:26:39.580
Uh, well...

00:26:40.040 --> 00:26:41.290
You see, um...

00:26:41.370 --> 00:26:43.080
Hey, your eye color!

00:26:43.950 --> 00:26:45.080
What?

00:26:45.160 --> 00:26:47.450
It's really pretty.

00:26:47.540 --> 00:26:49.370
It's a bit blue, like a foreigner...

00:26:49.450 --> 00:26:50.950
Leave me alone!

00:26:52.790 --> 00:26:53.790
You fat pig!

00:26:56.870 --> 00:26:57.790
Fat...

00:26:59.790 --> 00:27:01.790
Uh... I mean...

00:27:03.750 --> 00:27:05.950
I see what you mean by normal.

00:27:07.950 --> 00:27:11.160
But there's no use
pretending to be normal.

00:27:11.620 --> 00:27:15.250
After all,
you look like just what you are.

00:27:18.330 --> 00:27:20.750
Okay, now let's drop it.

00:27:20.830 --> 00:27:23.000
You should join us next--

00:27:24.660 --> 00:27:25.830
Anna!

00:27:26.500 --> 00:27:27.700
Hey, watch it!

00:27:38.080 --> 00:27:40.000
<i>Like just what I am...</i>

00:28:05.620 --> 00:28:07.290
<i>Like just what I am...</i>

00:28:08.580 --> 00:28:10.790
<i>Ugly, stupid,</i>

00:28:11.870 --> 00:28:13.200
<i>moody,</i>

00:28:13.540 --> 00:28:15.330
<i>unpleasant...</i>

00:28:17.790 --> 00:28:18.870
<i>That's why...</i>

00:28:20.660 --> 00:28:22.370
<i>I hate myself.</i>

00:28:24.700 --> 00:28:26.540
<i>That's why everyone...</i>

00:28:28.950 --> 00:28:33.950
We don't have long to live.
Typically, you're the ones who--

00:28:34.040 --> 00:28:36.040
Still talking about that?

00:28:36.330 --> 00:28:38.870
We already settled this matter.

00:28:38.950 --> 00:28:41.660
We're not blaming you. It's just that...

00:28:41.750 --> 00:28:45.000
I've already told you.
It's not about money.

00:28:45.080 --> 00:28:46.660
I feel bad for her, but--

00:28:46.750 --> 00:28:49.410
It'll be best for her if you two--

00:29:09.200 --> 00:29:10.580
I'd better get home.

00:29:35.950 --> 00:29:37.790
Did someone row it here?

00:30:36.450 --> 00:30:37.500
It's stuck!

00:30:44.540 --> 00:30:45.660
Throw me the rope!

00:30:46.290 --> 00:30:47.540
The rope?

00:30:51.120 --> 00:30:52.200
Hurry!

00:31:23.160 --> 00:31:24.250
Are you okay?

00:31:25.830 --> 00:31:28.620
Yeah. Oh, um...

00:31:30.450 --> 00:31:32.290
Are you a real person?

00:31:32.790 --> 00:31:34.580
Don't let anyone hear us.

00:31:35.620 --> 00:31:38.450
You look like the girl I saw in my dreams.

00:31:39.250 --> 00:31:40.290
Dreams?

00:31:54.870 --> 00:31:55.950
Thanks.

00:32:00.450 --> 00:32:01.790
It's not a dream.

00:32:08.120 --> 00:32:10.500
What's your name?

00:32:11.000 --> 00:32:12.160
Anna.

00:32:12.250 --> 00:32:15.120
I hope we can be friends.

00:32:15.910 --> 00:32:17.000
What about you?

00:32:18.160 --> 00:32:19.120
Yes.

00:32:20.830 --> 00:32:22.620
Have you seen me before?

00:32:23.660 --> 00:32:24.830
Yes.

00:32:25.250 --> 00:32:26.500
Often.

00:32:27.500 --> 00:32:31.830
I just got here.
How long have you been here?

00:32:31.910 --> 00:32:33.830
I've been here for ages...

00:32:49.000 --> 00:32:51.580
Look at this, the marsh at night.

00:32:52.200 --> 00:32:56.620
How beautiful.
Say, let's go down for a closer look.

00:32:56.700 --> 00:32:57.450
Madam.

00:32:58.450 --> 00:33:00.040
I know.

00:33:00.370 --> 00:33:03.620
By the way, where's that child?

00:33:03.700 --> 00:33:06.040
Was she not in her room?

00:33:10.200 --> 00:33:11.540
I need to get back.

00:33:12.040 --> 00:33:14.080
-Were they talking about you?
-Yes.

00:33:16.540 --> 00:33:19.540
At this hour, I'm usually in bed.

00:33:22.120 --> 00:33:24.540
Come on, I'll row you back.

00:33:25.830 --> 00:33:27.080
So it was your boat.

00:33:28.040 --> 00:33:30.700
Yes, I left it for you on purpose.

00:33:34.750 --> 00:33:37.580
But I thought
you'd be able to row a little better.

00:33:40.160 --> 00:33:43.080
I know. So did I.

00:33:45.700 --> 00:33:48.080
You're my precious secret.

00:33:49.250 --> 00:33:52.450
I haven't told anyone about you,
and I won't.

00:33:53.080 --> 00:33:56.450
If someone finds out,
they'll only spoil it.

00:34:03.700 --> 00:34:06.410
Please, promise me...

00:34:07.660 --> 00:34:09.200
that we'll remain a secret.

00:34:09.910 --> 00:34:11.080
Forever.

00:34:12.700 --> 00:34:13.580
Yes.

00:34:15.290 --> 00:34:16.580
It'll be our secret.

00:34:17.080 --> 00:34:17.790
Forever.

00:35:00.660 --> 00:35:04.330
It was awful.
She came home crying her eyes out!

00:35:05.500 --> 00:35:07.040
Did Anna do something?

00:35:07.120 --> 00:35:09.830
She called my daughter a fat pig!

00:35:10.160 --> 00:35:11.830
Fat pig?

00:35:12.750 --> 00:35:16.700
And she pulled out a knife, too.
The horror!

00:35:16.790 --> 00:35:17.580
I doubt she'd--

00:35:18.160 --> 00:35:20.950
No, you need to hear it
from the girl herself.

00:35:21.040 --> 00:35:22.580
Now bring her here.

00:35:23.660 --> 00:35:25.830
Seems she's not home yet.

00:35:27.410 --> 00:35:30.580
She's a delinquent,
out and about this late!

00:35:31.120 --> 00:35:33.830
You two are at fault, too!

00:35:34.660 --> 00:35:36.830
Better keep an eye on her.

00:35:40.700 --> 00:35:42.080
Take this. It's dark.

00:35:42.160 --> 00:35:43.540
No, thank you.

00:35:46.290 --> 00:35:49.540
What if something happens
to one of the kids?

00:35:52.040 --> 00:35:53.950
So what if she's a bit late!

00:35:54.040 --> 00:35:55.500
Don't get so riled up.

00:35:55.580 --> 00:35:57.870
She is not a delinquent.

00:35:59.200 --> 00:36:00.870
Ah, she's home.

00:36:01.700 --> 00:36:03.040
Anna.

00:36:04.370 --> 00:36:05.290
Aunt Oiwa...

00:36:05.370 --> 00:36:08.660
Were you listening? Don't you worry.

00:36:10.540 --> 00:36:12.290
You two'll make up.

00:36:13.120 --> 00:36:15.540
Now take a bath and have dinner.

00:36:15.950 --> 00:36:16.700
Thank you.

00:36:16.790 --> 00:36:20.000
Or is it dinner before the bath?

00:36:20.080 --> 00:36:22.000
It hardly matters.

00:36:23.330 --> 00:36:25.500
But "fat pig" is a bit harsh.

00:36:27.330 --> 00:36:28.500
That's for sure.

00:36:28.830 --> 00:36:30.330
It's not that funny.

00:36:48.250 --> 00:36:50.830
Auntie, worrying like always.

00:36:55.080 --> 00:36:57.540
Anna! Watermelon!

00:37:02.830 --> 00:37:04.500
Anna?

00:37:07.330 --> 00:37:10.500
Two hours until high tide...

00:37:54.870 --> 00:37:56.910
Hop in. Time for a picnic.

00:37:57.660 --> 00:37:59.410
I brought juice and cookies.

00:37:59.870 --> 00:38:02.620
Picnic? At this hour?

00:38:02.700 --> 00:38:05.540
That's right.
Let's go to the other side of the marsh.

00:38:18.370 --> 00:38:20.080
You're very good at rowing.

00:38:22.370 --> 00:38:24.080
You need rowing lessons.

00:38:24.580 --> 00:38:25.660
Come here.

00:38:30.750 --> 00:38:31.750
It's easy.

00:38:39.120 --> 00:38:43.950
Remember I said last night
that you're my precious secret?

00:38:45.910 --> 00:38:49.290
I remember. And you're my secret.

00:38:49.750 --> 00:38:51.120
I'm glad.

00:38:52.700 --> 00:38:53.950
Hey!

00:38:59.290 --> 00:39:01.620
Good, you're doing well.

00:39:05.790 --> 00:39:09.040
But I don't even know your name yet.

00:39:12.450 --> 00:39:14.200
I haven't told you yet?

00:39:15.330 --> 00:39:16.250
Marnie.

00:39:16.660 --> 00:39:18.500
I thought you already knew.

00:39:20.500 --> 00:39:21.830
That's dangerous.

00:39:30.580 --> 00:39:32.950
Go ahead, just row.

00:39:49.700 --> 00:39:53.330
There's so much I want to know about you.

00:39:54.040 --> 00:39:56.660
But I don't wish to find out too fast.

00:39:57.700 --> 00:40:00.040
Let's take it slow, as we go along.

00:40:00.700 --> 00:40:01.540
Okay.

00:40:02.040 --> 00:40:04.410
I'll tell you what we'll do.

00:40:04.910 --> 00:40:09.500
We'll ask each other
three questions a night.

00:40:09.580 --> 00:40:10.410
Great.

00:40:11.040 --> 00:40:13.250
All right, I'll start.

00:40:13.330 --> 00:40:17.160
Question one.
Why are you here in this village?

00:40:18.200 --> 00:40:20.000
I have asthma.

00:40:20.080 --> 00:40:25.040
The doctor said I should go somewhere
with clean air for a while.

00:40:25.830 --> 00:40:27.660
Even if I have to skip school.

00:40:27.750 --> 00:40:29.330
Oh no, you're ill?

00:40:29.410 --> 00:40:31.040
If there's no attack, I'm fine.

00:40:31.750 --> 00:40:35.750
So I'm staying here
with Auntie's relatives, the Oiwas.

00:40:36.080 --> 00:40:37.200
Who's Auntie?

00:40:37.290 --> 00:40:39.040
It's my turn to ask a question.

00:40:39.750 --> 00:40:41.910
Do you live in that mansion?

00:40:42.750 --> 00:40:44.700
Ever since I was two.

00:40:45.120 --> 00:40:46.950
With Nan and the maids.

00:40:47.870 --> 00:40:48.910
It's juice.

00:40:49.790 --> 00:40:51.910
Where are your parents?

00:40:52.790 --> 00:40:56.580
They only come here sometimes.
They're busy with work.

00:40:56.950 --> 00:40:58.120
I see.

00:40:58.200 --> 00:41:01.080
Question two. Who's Auntie?

00:41:02.750 --> 00:41:03.910
My guardian.

00:41:04.870 --> 00:41:10.160
But I make her worry too much
so she got rid of me for a while.

00:41:10.250 --> 00:41:11.500
What do you mean?

00:41:12.000 --> 00:41:13.790
I'll explain another time.

00:41:14.450 --> 00:41:15.910
It's my turn now.

00:41:17.000 --> 00:41:18.370
Do you have siblings?

00:41:18.450 --> 00:41:19.910
I'm an only child.

00:41:20.000 --> 00:41:21.910
I see, you too...

00:41:22.000 --> 00:41:23.000
How come?

00:41:24.450 --> 00:41:26.040
Oh, it's nothing.

00:41:26.790 --> 00:41:30.040
Just curious what it's like
to have siblings.

00:41:30.790 --> 00:41:34.120
I know.
It's fun to imagine what it's like.

00:41:34.450 --> 00:41:36.040
All right, question three.

00:41:36.660 --> 00:41:39.330
What's it like living with the Oiwas?

00:41:40.000 --> 00:41:41.040
At the Oiwas?

00:41:44.450 --> 00:41:45.540
<i>Huh...</i>

00:41:46.790 --> 00:41:48.000
<i>How strange...</i>

00:41:49.120 --> 00:41:50.290
<i>I can't...</i>

00:41:51.330 --> 00:41:52.660
<i>remember...</i>

00:42:29.370 --> 00:42:30.410
Marnie?

00:42:34.080 --> 00:42:35.290
Marnie!

00:42:35.370 --> 00:42:36.450
Anna!

00:42:38.750 --> 00:42:42.580
There you are.
I was wondering where you went.

00:42:45.700 --> 00:42:46.910
Marnie?

00:42:52.200 --> 00:42:55.910
I was looking for you everywhere.
You just disappeared.

00:42:56.700 --> 00:42:58.410
I didn't go anywhere.

00:42:58.500 --> 00:43:00.910
I was just trying to answer your question.

00:43:02.200 --> 00:43:03.450
Wait...

00:43:04.250 --> 00:43:05.540
What was it?

00:43:06.660 --> 00:43:08.790
It's okay, it doesn't matter.

00:43:08.870 --> 00:43:11.200
I need to go soon. Today is...

00:43:14.330 --> 00:43:15.290
Oh, I know!

00:43:17.040 --> 00:43:21.500
No, no, no, I really can't!
Parties aren't really my--

00:43:21.580 --> 00:43:22.910
Don't worry.

00:43:24.000 --> 00:43:25.910
I have a great idea.

00:44:01.120 --> 00:44:02.660
It's true.

00:44:02.750 --> 00:44:04.290
That's hard to believe.

00:44:16.950 --> 00:44:21.120
Sorry, did you wait long?
I had trouble getting away.

00:44:21.580 --> 00:44:22.950
Marnie.

00:44:24.410 --> 00:44:25.450
What do you think?

00:44:26.450 --> 00:44:27.950
It's pretty.

00:44:28.830 --> 00:44:32.830
I borrowed Nan's shawl.
I'll be scolded again.

00:44:33.620 --> 00:44:34.750
This won't work.

00:44:35.120 --> 00:44:37.620
Don't worry, I spoke to Father.

00:44:44.290 --> 00:44:45.500
Young lady.

00:44:47.000 --> 00:44:49.500
I believe it is past your bedtime.

00:44:50.160 --> 00:44:52.160
And who might this be?

00:44:54.790 --> 00:44:56.700
She is wearing my shawl.

00:44:58.870 --> 00:44:59.660
Upstairs!

00:45:01.330 --> 00:45:02.700
Wait right there!

00:45:16.370 --> 00:45:19.160
You are nothing but trouble.

00:45:20.080 --> 00:45:21.200
You go that way.

00:45:24.910 --> 00:45:26.200
Marnie!

00:45:27.580 --> 00:45:28.700
Why you little--

00:45:39.700 --> 00:45:42.500
Marnie! Open it!

00:45:42.580 --> 00:45:43.500
Let's go.

00:45:43.580 --> 00:45:45.450
If you keep this up,

00:45:45.540 --> 00:45:47.950
you'll grow up to be a lousy adult!

00:45:55.620 --> 00:45:58.950
Everyone,
we have a lovely flower girl here.

00:45:59.910 --> 00:46:01.500
A guest of my daughter.

00:46:01.580 --> 00:46:03.080
Ah, a flower girl.

00:46:03.160 --> 00:46:06.450
-There's Marnie.
-She'll be pretty like her mother.

00:46:06.540 --> 00:46:10.120
May I please have one of those flowers?

00:46:11.580 --> 00:46:12.750
My mother.

00:46:20.750 --> 00:46:24.080
Hello, my dear little witch.

00:46:25.250 --> 00:46:28.080
That woman there is the real witch.

00:46:30.700 --> 00:46:31.910
Um...

00:46:37.700 --> 00:46:40.750
I want only one, for good luck.

00:46:41.700 --> 00:46:45.450
Will someone kindly pay for my flower?

00:46:48.120 --> 00:46:50.450
If it is the witch's command...

00:46:51.250 --> 00:46:52.950
Then I'll have one, too.

00:46:53.450 --> 00:46:55.620
-Here.
-For superb luck.

00:46:59.620 --> 00:47:01.000
Ah, it's begun.

00:47:06.290 --> 00:47:07.370
I'm sorry!

00:47:07.450 --> 00:47:08.370
Oh, she ran away.

00:47:24.290 --> 00:47:26.620
Come on and take one for good luck!

00:47:26.700 --> 00:47:27.950
May I have one, please?

00:47:43.870 --> 00:47:44.870
Young lady.

00:47:45.500 --> 00:47:47.500
To your health.

00:47:49.500 --> 00:47:51.160
Thank you.

00:48:11.250 --> 00:48:12.370
Wine?

00:48:24.370 --> 00:48:25.620
Are you awake yet?

00:48:28.160 --> 00:48:29.250
I...

00:48:30.700 --> 00:48:32.080
You drunkard.

00:48:35.500 --> 00:48:36.950
Who was that?

00:48:37.290 --> 00:48:38.500
Who?

00:48:38.580 --> 00:48:40.040
The one who was dancing with you.

00:48:41.080 --> 00:48:44.200
Kazuhiko? He's an old friend.

00:48:45.870 --> 00:48:47.750
He's a good dancer.

00:48:48.910 --> 00:48:50.040
So are you.

00:48:54.290 --> 00:48:57.000
Now let's dance, you and I.

00:49:01.120 --> 00:49:03.200
I can't dance.

00:49:03.290 --> 00:49:05.120
Just follow my lead.

00:50:02.500 --> 00:50:04.500
Look for me again.

00:50:05.660 --> 00:50:09.080
And don't tell anyone. Promise.

00:50:09.160 --> 00:50:10.000
I know.

00:50:13.370 --> 00:50:15.370
Hey, wait...

00:50:34.790 --> 00:50:35.870
Is that--

00:50:40.870 --> 00:50:42.870
It's the girl with the Oiwas.

00:51:04.750 --> 00:51:05.750
DEAR ANNA, HOW ARE YOU?
IT SEEMS LIKE YOU'RE ENJOYING IT...

00:51:05.830 --> 00:51:07.660
I HOPE TO HEAR FROM YOU SOON. YORIKO.

00:51:13.040 --> 00:51:16.040
I see. I hope you find the other shoe.

00:51:16.910 --> 00:51:18.700
It must be somewhere.

00:51:19.200 --> 00:51:20.700
I'll go look for it.

00:51:21.540 --> 00:51:23.040
I used to always lose mine.

00:51:23.700 --> 00:51:26.830
There's a bunch of shoes
buried in the mudflats.

00:51:26.910 --> 00:51:28.910
Don't compare her to you.

00:51:29.250 --> 00:51:32.200
I should have my daughter's old shoes.

00:51:32.660 --> 00:51:34.080
I'll get them out.

00:51:34.750 --> 00:51:36.250
Thank you.

00:51:54.580 --> 00:51:55.750
Marnie...

00:52:31.000 --> 00:52:32.290
Wow.

00:52:33.910 --> 00:52:37.660
Not only are they big,
they're delicious, too.

00:52:54.250 --> 00:52:56.540
You're good with the knife.

00:52:56.620 --> 00:52:59.080
Auntie teaches me all the time.

00:52:59.540 --> 00:53:03.200
You're so polite and well-behaved.

00:53:03.700 --> 00:53:06.040
My daughter could learn from you.

00:53:07.540 --> 00:53:08.910
Passing behind you.

00:53:09.540 --> 00:53:13.250
I remember when you first came
to Yoriko's place.

00:53:14.080 --> 00:53:15.910
She was ecstatic.

00:53:17.000 --> 00:53:22.910
She wanted to make up for the five years
she didn't have with you.

00:53:24.410 --> 00:53:28.580
So she taught you things,
like knife skills.

00:53:32.910 --> 00:53:35.040
But she worries too much.

00:53:36.540 --> 00:53:38.830
Always calling me for help.

00:53:38.910 --> 00:53:42.330
When I told her I was busy,
she started pouting.

00:53:42.410 --> 00:53:44.870
Oh, I shouldn't share this
about your mother.

00:53:46.580 --> 00:53:48.250
No, I understand.

00:53:48.750 --> 00:53:52.870
You know,
Yoriko sent us tons of photos of you.

00:53:53.950 --> 00:53:55.290
I'll show you later.

00:53:58.750 --> 00:53:59.950
Hey, look.

00:54:01.120 --> 00:54:03.870
Found the wind chime
I made on our honeymoon.

00:54:05.410 --> 00:54:07.580
To survive the summer.

00:54:10.080 --> 00:54:12.080
Your hair's getting long.

00:54:12.540 --> 00:54:14.620
Shall I give you a haircut?

00:54:14.950 --> 00:54:16.950
That would be a disaster.

00:54:44.160 --> 00:54:46.000
Mar... nie...

00:54:46.950 --> 00:54:48.540
<i>Look for me again.</i>

00:54:55.000 --> 00:54:58.040
<i>How could I nearly forget about Marnie?</i>

00:55:14.910 --> 00:55:16.040
<i>Marnie...</i>

00:55:21.040 --> 00:55:22.080
<i>Marnie!</i>

00:55:27.700 --> 00:55:29.040
Marnie...

00:56:07.040 --> 00:56:08.450
May I?

00:56:10.580 --> 00:56:11.580
Sure.

00:56:12.450 --> 00:56:14.500
I see you draw, too.

00:56:15.080 --> 00:56:18.040
That girl looks like someone I knew.

00:56:18.120 --> 00:56:19.790
She was a great girl.

00:56:21.580 --> 00:56:23.450
Yes, she is.

00:56:24.080 --> 00:56:27.500
But I haven't seen her in a week.

00:56:29.000 --> 00:56:32.790
I wonder if she's upset that I forgot.

00:56:34.160 --> 00:56:37.450
If she's a friend,
talk to her and you'll be fine.

00:56:39.250 --> 00:56:41.120
Say, will you take a look?

00:56:41.790 --> 00:56:42.790
Sure.

00:56:51.290 --> 00:56:53.700
Are the colors too messy?

00:56:53.790 --> 00:56:56.080
No, it's wonderful.

00:56:56.450 --> 00:56:58.040
I'm Hisako.

00:56:58.120 --> 00:57:01.830
I'm in love with the marsh house.
What about you?

00:57:03.250 --> 00:57:05.870
I'm Anna. I love it, too.

00:57:12.830 --> 00:57:16.040
Better hurry and finish your drawing...

00:57:16.500 --> 00:57:18.330
before the new folks move in.

00:57:18.660 --> 00:57:20.830
The renovations are under way.

00:57:24.660 --> 00:57:27.950
Thanks for your hard work. Have some tea.

00:57:28.040 --> 00:57:30.660
Oh, thank you. Appreciate it.

00:57:32.330 --> 00:57:34.080
Hey, let's take a break!

00:57:34.160 --> 00:57:36.040
All right, coming.

00:57:48.040 --> 00:57:49.700
Are you Marnie?

00:57:55.750 --> 00:57:56.790
Come.

00:58:11.200 --> 00:58:13.870
I hadn't seen the front before.

00:58:14.250 --> 00:58:17.120
It's a lot cleaner now,
but it's not finished yet.

00:58:19.370 --> 00:58:20.910
Hello.

00:58:21.000 --> 00:58:22.290
Hey there.

00:58:22.370 --> 00:58:24.370
You brought a friend, huh?

00:58:25.750 --> 00:58:27.700
Choose your slippers.

00:58:28.450 --> 00:58:29.500
A guest?

00:58:29.580 --> 00:58:30.500
Yeah, a secret one.

00:58:31.080 --> 00:58:32.330
Secret?

00:58:32.410 --> 00:58:33.750
Hey!

00:58:34.120 --> 00:58:36.500
Sorry, make yourself at home.

00:58:37.950 --> 00:58:39.580
Thank you.

00:58:43.580 --> 00:58:46.450
Yes, it's a lovely place.

00:58:46.540 --> 00:58:49.870
Yes, we haven't finished renovating.

00:58:50.540 --> 00:58:51.950
This room...

00:58:55.250 --> 00:58:56.370
Upstairs.

00:58:58.080 --> 00:59:00.160
This hasn't been renovated yet.

00:59:04.410 --> 00:59:06.410
Here, this is my room.

00:59:09.250 --> 00:59:10.450
Really...

00:59:15.080 --> 00:59:16.200
What do you think?

00:59:16.290 --> 00:59:18.870
It's a cute room.

00:59:20.620 --> 00:59:23.120
It used to be your room, right?

00:59:24.620 --> 00:59:25.790
You're...

00:59:26.660 --> 00:59:27.830
Marnie, right?

00:59:28.450 --> 00:59:31.200
Me? No, no!

00:59:31.290 --> 00:59:35.250
But... then why have you been staring
at my room?

00:59:35.330 --> 00:59:36.080
Because--

00:59:36.160 --> 00:59:39.120
See, that's where I always see you.

00:59:39.870 --> 00:59:42.200
I've seen you many times.

00:59:44.160 --> 00:59:45.250
No, no.

00:59:46.000 --> 00:59:48.700
I just love this mansion, that's all.

00:59:48.790 --> 00:59:49.790
That can't be.

00:59:51.000 --> 00:59:54.450
When I said Marnie earlier,
you were surprised.

00:59:54.540 --> 00:59:57.410
Rather, why do you know Marnie?

01:00:02.200 --> 01:00:04.160
I found it behind the shelf.

01:00:06.080 --> 01:00:07.080
A diary?

01:00:07.160 --> 01:00:09.830
That's right. Your diary.

01:00:17.660 --> 01:00:19.040
Marnie!

01:00:21.040 --> 01:00:24.540
I'll pour you some Queen Mary,
your favorite.

01:00:25.450 --> 01:00:26.750
I'll be back.

01:00:32.830 --> 01:00:35.540
<i>"Last night I went</i>
<i>for a row in my nightie.</i>

01:00:37.080 --> 01:00:40.580
<i>The marsh and the moon</i>
<i>were very pretty at night."</i>

01:00:41.620 --> 01:00:43.290
<i>I shall do it again.</i>

01:00:46.000 --> 01:00:48.700
<i>June 8th. A party!</i>

01:00:49.580 --> 01:00:54.540
<i>Father, Mother and many of their friends</i>
<i>came over. It was such fun.</i>

01:00:56.410 --> 01:00:58.080
<i>I went outside from the sunroom</i>

01:00:58.910 --> 01:01:02.250
<i>and danced with a flower girl.</i>

01:01:04.660 --> 01:01:05.620
<i>But...</i>

01:01:06.500 --> 01:01:10.910
<i>Nan locked me in my room</i>
<i>because of last night.</i>

01:01:12.250 --> 01:01:16.040
<i>So there won't be</i>
<i>any midnight rows for a while.</i>

01:01:23.790 --> 01:01:26.410
See, it's you, isn't it?

01:01:28.750 --> 01:01:29.950
No.

01:01:30.790 --> 01:01:31.870
Marnie is...

01:01:32.660 --> 01:01:34.080
Marnie is...

01:01:34.950 --> 01:01:37.790
someone I made up.

01:01:39.410 --> 01:01:42.580
An imaginary girl, only in my mind.

01:01:43.950 --> 01:01:46.790
But this is Marnie's diary.

01:01:48.000 --> 01:01:51.000
It's as if she really lived here.

01:01:53.750 --> 01:01:56.200
So you're not Marnie?

01:01:56.290 --> 01:01:57.120
No.

01:01:57.200 --> 01:01:59.120
She's just imaginary?

01:01:59.450 --> 01:02:00.200
That's right.

01:02:02.790 --> 01:02:06.500
I thought you were Marnie,
and you came back for the diary...

01:02:10.620 --> 01:02:13.950
I'm Anna.
I came from Sapporo to get better.

01:02:14.580 --> 01:02:16.540
I'm Sayaka.

01:02:17.120 --> 01:02:19.200
I'm from Tokyo.

01:02:20.450 --> 01:02:25.290
But if she was imaginary,
why is the name in the diary the same?

01:02:26.450 --> 01:02:27.700
I don't know.

01:02:28.160 --> 01:02:32.660
Marnie must be real.
I'm going to investigate.

01:02:45.910 --> 01:02:48.910
<i>Tell me, Marnie...</i>

01:02:50.330 --> 01:02:53.410
<i>Who are you?</i>

01:03:15.250 --> 01:03:16.370
Is that me?

01:03:24.580 --> 01:03:25.830
Marnie?

01:03:26.290 --> 01:03:27.580
Marnie!

01:03:32.790 --> 01:03:33.790
Um...

01:03:39.080 --> 01:03:43.290
Wait, that one's not finished yet...

01:03:43.950 --> 01:03:46.290
Wow, you draw well.

01:03:46.370 --> 01:03:48.330
Oh, thanks...

01:03:48.410 --> 01:03:53.080
I've never had anyone
draw me before. How nice!

01:04:01.580 --> 01:04:03.000
I missed you.

01:04:05.910 --> 01:04:08.450
I kept calling you in my heart.

01:04:12.790 --> 01:04:13.790
Me, too.

01:04:14.450 --> 01:04:15.370
Let's go.

01:04:15.450 --> 01:04:16.540
Come to my room.

01:04:17.830 --> 01:04:20.660
Come to my room, Marnie.

01:04:23.450 --> 01:04:26.830
I can't go very far from the mansion.

01:04:28.910 --> 01:04:33.160
Okay then, we'll go wherever you want.

01:05:02.700 --> 01:05:04.750
<i>You know a lot about mushrooms.</i>

01:05:05.540 --> 01:05:08.660
<i>Father taught me when I was little.</i>

01:05:09.000 --> 01:05:12.500
<i>I once brought home</i>
<i>three bags full of mushrooms.</i>

01:05:13.870 --> 01:05:16.330
The look on Mother's face!

01:05:25.040 --> 01:05:26.790
What's wrong?

01:05:26.870 --> 01:05:28.370
You're so quiet all of a sudden.

01:05:30.540 --> 01:05:32.540
You're very lucky.

01:05:32.910 --> 01:05:35.910
I wish I was you.

01:05:45.830 --> 01:05:46.950
Talk to me.

01:05:50.160 --> 01:05:51.370
I'm...

01:05:53.330 --> 01:05:54.790
a foster child.

01:05:56.910 --> 01:06:00.580
My real parents died when I was little.

01:06:01.580 --> 01:06:02.700
My grandmother, too.

01:06:03.830 --> 01:06:06.950
I know they didn't die on purpose, but...

01:06:07.910 --> 01:06:09.450
sometimes I feel like...

01:06:10.950 --> 01:06:12.250
I can't forgive them...

01:06:12.950 --> 01:06:15.290
for leaving me all alone.

01:06:20.080 --> 01:06:21.660
I'm jealous of you.

01:06:22.080 --> 01:06:24.500
You're lucky to be a foster child.

01:06:25.370 --> 01:06:27.500
If you had no relatives,

01:06:28.080 --> 01:06:31.500
then the folks
who took you in as a daughter

01:06:32.250 --> 01:06:34.790
must be truly kindhearted people.

01:06:45.950 --> 01:06:48.580
Then I'll tell you a big secret.

01:06:49.950 --> 01:06:55.580
It's about my foster parents.
They're good to me and they're kind.

01:06:56.500 --> 01:07:01.370
I'm not their real child,
yet they raised me, which I appreciate.

01:07:03.660 --> 01:07:06.450
But you see, I saw it one day.

01:07:07.120 --> 01:07:10.000
They're paid to look after me.

01:07:11.120 --> 01:07:12.620
<i>Paid?</i>

01:07:13.000 --> 01:07:15.540
<i>I found a letter from the government.</i>

01:07:17.580 --> 01:07:21.790
<i>It said they were increasing</i>
<i>the subsidy for me.</i>

01:07:23.500 --> 01:07:25.410
<i>I'm sure there's a reason--</i>

01:07:25.500 --> 01:07:27.330
<i>I don't care!</i>

01:07:29.200 --> 01:07:33.790
<i>They wouldn't get money</i>
<i>if I were their real child.</i>

01:07:35.080 --> 01:07:39.200
<i>They get paid</i>
<i>because I'm not their real child.</i>

01:07:41.540 --> 01:07:46.910
<i>Even worse... they hide it from me.</i>

01:07:48.700 --> 01:07:50.040
I see.

01:07:51.580 --> 01:07:55.410
But that doesn't mean
Auntie doesn't love you.

01:07:55.500 --> 01:07:58.160
No! Don't you see?

01:07:58.250 --> 01:08:02.410
None of the other families
receive money. Just us!

01:08:03.200 --> 01:08:07.910
She always looks worried
that I might find out.

01:08:08.250 --> 01:08:11.950
And I hate myself for thinking like this.

01:08:12.790 --> 01:08:16.080
I... just can't... believe...

01:08:16.160 --> 01:08:18.120
in anything anymore.

01:08:28.120 --> 01:08:31.040
Anna, it's okay to cry.

01:08:31.120 --> 01:08:33.120
Just know that I love you.

01:08:35.330 --> 01:08:39.540
I love you more than any girl
I've ever known.

01:08:42.450 --> 01:08:45.330
Then you tell me your secret.

01:08:48.910 --> 01:08:52.830
A long time ago,
I went mushrooming with Father.

01:08:54.160 --> 01:08:57.200
Nowadays, I hardly see my parents.

01:08:59.000 --> 01:09:00.910
<i>Mother's usually travelling.</i>

01:09:05.950 --> 01:09:09.500
<i>Because of work,</i>
<i>Father's home only twice a year.</i>

01:09:10.950 --> 01:09:15.330
<i>Usually, Nan and the twin maids</i>
<i>are the only ones home.</i>

01:09:15.660 --> 01:09:17.750
<i>With me.</i>

01:09:19.000 --> 01:09:21.910
<i>I slip out while they're gossiping.</i>

01:09:22.330 --> 01:09:26.250
<i>And look how free I get to be!</i>

01:09:29.620 --> 01:09:32.870
It's so lovely when my parents come home.

01:09:33.620 --> 01:09:35.160
They host parties!

01:09:36.160 --> 01:09:38.200
Like the other day.

01:09:39.370 --> 01:09:41.700
With my amazing parents

01:09:41.790 --> 01:09:45.450
and many people there, it's delightful.

01:09:46.160 --> 01:09:49.700
I get to wear new dresses and dance, too.

01:09:51.370 --> 01:09:56.410
That's when I feel
I'm the luckiest girl in the world.

01:09:57.910 --> 01:09:59.120
I see.

01:10:09.370 --> 01:10:13.950
Tell me, Anna.
Will you be my friend forever?

01:10:14.700 --> 01:10:15.750
Yes.

01:10:15.830 --> 01:10:17.540
I'm your friend forever.

01:10:18.950 --> 01:10:20.450
Right?

01:10:24.200 --> 01:10:26.450
<i>Nan's always in a bad mood.</i>

01:10:26.540 --> 01:10:31.160
<i>She yanks me by the arm,</i>
<i>brushes my hair very hard...</i>

01:10:32.080 --> 01:10:34.250
<i>No one thinks I'm being bullied.</i>

01:10:35.080 --> 01:10:36.750
<i>But it really hurts.</i>

01:10:37.750 --> 01:10:38.950
Enough to cry.

01:10:41.450 --> 01:10:43.950
The maids love to frighten me.

01:10:45.250 --> 01:10:47.540
They threatened me all the time.

01:10:48.790 --> 01:10:50.830
"Naughty kids get locked up in the silo

01:10:51.250 --> 01:10:54.290
where ghosts suck out their souls,"
they said.

01:10:55.660 --> 01:10:58.250
You mean, the silo on the hill?

01:10:58.580 --> 01:11:01.790
Once, they actually took me there.

01:11:02.660 --> 01:11:03.580
No!

01:11:03.660 --> 01:11:06.540
<i>They dragged me all the way to the silo.</i>

01:11:07.000 --> 01:11:08.830
<i>I thought I'd die of fright.</i>

01:11:09.330 --> 01:11:10.660
<i>Then suddenly,</i>

01:11:10.750 --> 01:11:14.870
<i>just as we got there, the sky</i>
<i>went dark and a storm broke out.</i>

01:11:18.790 --> 01:11:21.830
<i>The maids were terrified,</i>
<i>so we didn't go inside.</i>

01:11:23.200 --> 01:11:26.290
I can endure anything else.

01:11:27.330 --> 01:11:30.160
Anything but the silo.

01:11:30.950 --> 01:11:33.950
I have never heard such a terrible thing!

01:11:34.040 --> 01:11:37.200
I hope the maids and Nan
get struck by lightning!

01:11:39.330 --> 01:11:43.290
Hasn't anyone ever tried to frighten you?

01:11:43.910 --> 01:11:46.700
Never. Definitely not on purpose.

01:11:48.410 --> 01:11:50.250
You're lucky.

01:11:51.290 --> 01:11:53.580
I wish I was you.

01:11:56.200 --> 01:11:57.750
Our castle...

01:12:00.660 --> 01:12:02.540
Poor Marnie.

01:12:03.080 --> 01:12:05.620
I love you so much.

01:12:05.950 --> 01:12:08.080
More than anyone I've known.

01:12:10.540 --> 01:12:11.790
Thank you.

01:12:17.410 --> 01:12:21.250
It's funny. It's like we traded places.

01:12:21.950 --> 01:12:23.580
How true.

01:12:30.790 --> 01:12:32.580
The tide's coming in.

01:12:33.830 --> 01:12:36.750
Hey, let's go to the silo together.

01:12:38.250 --> 01:12:41.950
The ghosts must be a lie.
Let's go make sure.

01:12:43.040 --> 01:12:46.250
Tomorrow... No, let's go right now.

01:12:53.370 --> 01:12:55.790
<i>I don't care who Marnie really is.</i>

01:12:57.250 --> 01:13:00.330
<i>I just want to help her.</i>

01:13:12.160 --> 01:13:14.000
Are you okay, Marnie?

01:13:14.830 --> 01:13:18.410
Yes, I'm sure
I'll be all right if I'm with you...

01:13:19.160 --> 01:13:20.290
Kazuhiko.

01:13:29.750 --> 01:13:31.830
Anna!

01:13:32.620 --> 01:13:35.540
Perfect timing! I found it!

01:13:45.660 --> 01:13:48.580
The rest of the diary. Come to my place.

01:13:49.040 --> 01:13:50.540
Marnie...

01:13:51.790 --> 01:13:54.580
I'm sorry. Another time.

01:13:55.040 --> 01:13:57.580
What? But it's a major discovery...

01:13:58.950 --> 01:14:01.200
It's going to rain!

01:14:55.450 --> 01:14:56.450
Who is it?

01:14:58.870 --> 01:15:00.200
Is someone there?

01:15:00.620 --> 01:15:01.950
Marnie!

01:15:06.120 --> 01:15:09.830
So you did go ahead.
Don't scare me like that.

01:15:12.700 --> 01:15:13.660
Marnie.

01:15:17.790 --> 01:15:19.790
Are you okay? Why did you--

01:15:19.870 --> 01:15:20.790
Kazuhiko!

01:15:22.200 --> 01:15:25.370
I'm scared. I heard somebody below.

01:15:26.200 --> 01:15:29.290
I thought I'd die of fright. Kazuhiko...

01:15:30.200 --> 01:15:34.500
What're you saying? I'm Anna.
Pull yourself together.

01:15:34.580 --> 01:15:37.040
Anna... Anna!

01:15:37.450 --> 01:15:40.120
I don't want to be humiliated.

01:15:40.200 --> 01:15:41.790
But I haven't the courage.

01:15:41.870 --> 01:15:43.040
Oh, Anna...

01:15:44.290 --> 01:15:47.040
You do have courage. You came here.

01:15:49.370 --> 01:15:50.370
Let's go home.

01:16:04.580 --> 01:16:05.750
Wait!

01:16:09.620 --> 01:16:12.200
It's just the wind. Let's go.

01:16:12.950 --> 01:16:14.790
We'll go home together.

01:16:30.040 --> 01:16:31.160
No...

01:16:34.160 --> 01:16:36.290
Anna, come back here.

01:16:36.660 --> 01:16:37.660
Anna!

01:16:38.540 --> 01:16:41.660
We got all the way up here.
I'm sure we can make it down.

01:16:42.620 --> 01:16:45.000
I'll go first, so follow me.

01:16:47.000 --> 01:16:49.660
No, don't leave me!

01:16:58.830 --> 01:16:59.660
No!

01:17:03.160 --> 01:17:04.330
Marnie!

01:17:06.330 --> 01:17:08.160
Let's go over there.

01:17:21.700 --> 01:17:24.200
I'm cold... So cold...

01:17:28.000 --> 01:17:32.200
Oh Anna, I'm scared... I'm scared...

01:17:32.540 --> 01:17:35.950
Don't worry,
we'll be fine if we're together.

01:17:36.040 --> 01:17:39.200
You did well, Marnie.

01:18:20.910 --> 01:18:22.250
Are you okay?

01:18:23.410 --> 01:18:24.750
Kazuhiko!

01:18:25.750 --> 01:18:27.620
<i>I thought you'd never come.</i>

01:18:28.750 --> 01:18:30.910
I... I...

01:18:39.040 --> 01:18:40.620
Let's go home.

01:19:05.290 --> 01:19:06.620
Marnie?

01:19:09.450 --> 01:19:10.950
Marnie!

01:19:17.950 --> 01:19:20.540
Marnie!

01:19:27.450 --> 01:19:30.950
<i>Marnie... You left me behind!</i>

01:19:37.870 --> 01:19:39.700
<i>Even you!</i>

01:20:06.040 --> 01:20:08.660
Kazuhiko... Kazuhiko...

01:20:09.120 --> 01:20:11.790
Kazuhiko's all over this diary.

01:20:13.500 --> 01:20:17.950
"Kazuhiko is trying
to take me to the silo."

01:20:18.580 --> 01:20:19.790
Silo...

01:20:22.580 --> 01:20:23.580
Yes?

01:20:25.040 --> 01:20:26.830
Mom cooked some corn.

01:20:27.450 --> 01:20:29.950
-Hurry or it'll be gone.
-Wait!

01:20:31.950 --> 01:20:34.450
Why go out on a night like this?

01:20:35.290 --> 01:20:36.410
It's not safe.

01:20:36.500 --> 01:20:41.290
My friend might be caught in the rain.
What if she gets pneumonia?

01:20:45.580 --> 01:20:46.700
Is that...

01:20:47.700 --> 01:20:48.950
Anna!

01:20:49.500 --> 01:20:50.500
Are you okay?

01:20:53.000 --> 01:20:54.160
So cruel...

01:20:55.660 --> 01:20:57.160
Anna?

01:20:58.700 --> 01:21:00.950
So cruel, Marnie...

01:21:01.500 --> 01:21:03.080
She has a high fever!

01:21:03.160 --> 01:21:04.500
I'll go get some help.

01:21:05.540 --> 01:21:07.000
Anna.

01:21:10.250 --> 01:21:11.330
Anna?

01:21:13.250 --> 01:21:14.660
Anna...

01:21:21.000 --> 01:21:22.500
How's she doing?

01:21:24.580 --> 01:21:26.370
Her fever's not coming down.

01:21:28.040 --> 01:21:30.370
<i>She did get a shot earlier.</i>

01:21:30.790 --> 01:21:32.200
<i>I see.</i>

01:21:43.700 --> 01:21:44.870
<i>So cruel...</i>

01:21:48.040 --> 01:21:50.540
Marnie, how could you?

01:21:55.200 --> 01:21:56.870
<i>I won't forgive you.</i>

01:21:58.160 --> 01:22:00.370
<i>Leaving me behind without a word.</i>

01:22:25.620 --> 01:22:28.370
Anna! My dear Anna!

01:22:30.410 --> 01:22:34.410
Marnie! How could you leave me behind?

01:22:35.000 --> 01:22:36.750
Why did you betray me?

01:22:37.580 --> 01:22:40.750
I'm sorry,
I didn't mean to leave you all alone.

01:22:41.910 --> 01:22:42.750
But...

01:22:45.120 --> 01:22:48.370
But at that moment, you weren't there.

01:22:50.000 --> 01:22:51.000
What do you mean?

01:22:51.790 --> 01:22:54.290
Oh, Anna, I...

01:22:55.250 --> 01:22:57.500
I can't stay here any longer.

01:22:58.120 --> 01:23:01.120
I have to say goodbye to you.

01:23:02.120 --> 01:23:06.200
So please, Anna,
please tell me you forgive me!

01:23:10.790 --> 01:23:12.040
Anna...

01:23:15.120 --> 01:23:17.620
Of course, I forgive you!

01:23:17.950 --> 01:23:20.370
I love you, Marnie!

01:23:20.790 --> 01:23:23.000
And I won't forget you!

01:23:23.450 --> 01:23:26.080
I'll never forget you! Ever!

01:24:08.120 --> 01:24:09.160
Anna.

01:24:16.250 --> 01:24:17.790
Sayaka's here for you.

01:24:21.410 --> 01:24:22.290
Thanks.

01:24:25.660 --> 01:24:27.950
You could see her in your room.

01:24:28.370 --> 01:24:30.750
No, it's nice outside.

01:24:30.830 --> 01:24:33.290
THE VIEW HERE IS BEAUTIFUL.
I'D LOVE TO SHOW YOU. ANNA

01:24:34.120 --> 01:24:35.540
Sayaka.

01:24:36.370 --> 01:24:38.120
Here, a get-well gift.

01:24:38.200 --> 01:24:39.580
Thanks.

01:24:39.660 --> 01:24:40.540
Also...

01:24:43.450 --> 01:24:47.790
This is what made me think
you might be at the silo.

01:24:47.870 --> 01:24:48.950
What is it?

01:24:49.040 --> 01:24:52.160
The rest of the diary
you promised to read.

01:24:53.200 --> 01:24:56.330
I'm having trouble remembering.

01:24:56.410 --> 01:24:57.910
I impressed myself.

01:24:58.540 --> 01:25:02.410
I found a clue in this painting
that was behind the cupboard.

01:25:03.660 --> 01:25:05.910
Maybe I'm psychic.

01:25:06.580 --> 01:25:08.080
Turn it over.

01:25:14.080 --> 01:25:15.410
Hisako!

01:25:18.830 --> 01:25:20.580
Hisako!

01:25:35.660 --> 01:25:39.120
Please, will you tell us about Marnie?

01:25:39.830 --> 01:25:40.620
But...

01:25:41.790 --> 01:25:43.620
it's a rather sad story.

01:25:44.450 --> 01:25:45.750
I'm ready for it.

01:25:50.580 --> 01:25:53.450
It was a long time ago.

01:25:55.160 --> 01:25:58.790
<i>I used to play at the marsh house often.</i>

01:26:00.790 --> 01:26:03.200
<i>Marnie and I were very little.</i>

01:26:03.290 --> 01:26:04.540
It's a bear!

01:26:04.620 --> 01:26:05.910
Let me see.

01:26:06.410 --> 01:26:09.450
This is Daddy. Isn't he dashing?

01:26:10.000 --> 01:26:12.250
<i>Marnie loved to boast</i>

01:26:12.330 --> 01:26:15.910
<i>about her glamorous parents</i>
<i>and their extravagant parties.</i>

01:26:19.250 --> 01:26:22.450
<i>But the truth is, she was being neglected.</i>

01:26:26.370 --> 01:26:28.370
Goodbye, Marnie.

01:26:28.450 --> 01:26:29.950
<i>That poor child...</i>

01:26:30.040 --> 01:26:35.160
No, don't leave me, Mommy! Don't go!

01:26:35.250 --> 01:26:38.200
<i>It seemed like even the maids</i>
<i>were bullying her.</i>

01:26:38.950 --> 01:26:40.290
That's awful!

01:26:41.540 --> 01:26:44.370
<i>Later, Marnie moved to Sapporo</i>

01:26:44.450 --> 01:26:47.290
<i>and married Kazuhiko,</i>
<i>her childhood friend.</i>

01:26:50.700 --> 01:26:54.120
<i>With her family torn apart</i>
<i>and feeling lost,</i>

01:26:54.200 --> 01:26:56.790
<i>he was there to support her.</i>

01:26:58.410 --> 01:27:02.540
<i>I'm glad. So Kazuhiko was a good man.</i>

01:27:04.410 --> 01:27:07.330
<i>Two years later, Emily was born.</i>

01:27:08.160 --> 01:27:13.660
<i>At last, in the warm household</i>
<i>she'd always wanted, Marnie was happy.</i>

01:27:16.160 --> 01:27:19.830
I didn't see Marnie
for many years after that.

01:27:21.120 --> 01:27:22.830
The next time was...

01:27:22.910 --> 01:27:27.000
a few years after Kazuhiko
had died of an illness.

01:27:29.700 --> 01:27:31.000
By then,

01:27:31.790 --> 01:27:37.040
Marnie was in a sanatorium
due to the shock of his death.

01:27:37.410 --> 01:27:38.870
Sanatorium?

01:27:39.500 --> 01:27:42.000
A place where you go to get better.

01:27:43.410 --> 01:27:45.580
What happened to Emily?

01:27:46.250 --> 01:27:51.250
Marnie's parents had died,
leaving no one to look after her.

01:27:54.120 --> 01:27:58.580
<i>So for elementary school,</i>
<i>she was sent to a boarding school.</i>

01:28:07.250 --> 01:28:12.080
<i>By the time she returned at age 13,</i>
<i>she'd become a different person.</i>

01:28:12.620 --> 01:28:13.950
Emily!

01:28:14.040 --> 01:28:16.750
<i>She was willful and independent.</i>

01:28:17.620 --> 01:28:19.250
<i>She knew Marnie was ill,</i>

01:28:19.330 --> 01:28:23.790
<i>but she still resented her</i>
<i>for sending her away.</i>

01:28:24.790 --> 01:28:27.750
You think that makes you more motherly?

01:28:27.830 --> 01:28:31.500
I want you to live the way
you wish, but...

01:28:32.000 --> 01:28:33.200
you need to...

01:28:33.290 --> 01:28:36.540
<i>They never did make up after that.</i>

01:28:36.620 --> 01:28:37.500
As your mother--

01:28:37.580 --> 01:28:40.620
I've never thought of you as a mother.

01:28:42.120 --> 01:28:45.950
<i>Emily ran away and soon got married.</i>

01:28:47.200 --> 01:28:49.290
<i>She was expecting, you see.</i>

01:29:09.830 --> 01:29:11.000
<i>But...</i>

01:29:13.330 --> 01:29:18.830
<i>One day, Emily and her husband</i>
<i>died in a car accident.</i>

01:29:22.080 --> 01:29:24.620
<i>I heard Marnie took their child in.</i>

01:29:26.870 --> 01:29:31.830
<i>She was determined to never</i>
<i>let this child be lonely.</i>

01:29:33.620 --> 01:29:34.500
<i>But...</i>

01:29:35.000 --> 01:29:38.620
<i>she never got over losing Emily.</i>

01:29:40.120 --> 01:29:44.370
<i>She became very ill</i>
<i>and died the following year.</i>

01:29:46.700 --> 01:29:49.700
<i>That was about ten years ago.</i>

01:29:55.250 --> 01:29:58.000
I'm sorry, it's a sad story.

01:29:58.080 --> 01:30:00.700
No, thank you very much.

01:30:02.200 --> 01:30:05.370
Marnie adored that mansion.

01:30:08.000 --> 01:30:11.370
She loved seeing the marsh
from her window.

01:30:13.080 --> 01:30:16.870
She said it felt like
the birds spoke to her.

01:30:18.870 --> 01:30:21.620
She had a lonely life,

01:30:21.700 --> 01:30:23.870
but she lived it fully.

01:30:24.750 --> 01:30:28.410
She always had a smile on her face.
She was determined to be happy.

01:30:31.080 --> 01:30:33.330
So you've met Marnie, too.

01:30:53.580 --> 01:30:56.700
<i>I wish we could've played more, Anna.</i>

01:30:57.080 --> 01:31:00.080
The plan was always
for me to stay just for the summer.

01:31:00.910 --> 01:31:02.950
Will you come back next summer?

01:31:03.370 --> 01:31:05.750
I'm sure I will. I'll write you.

01:31:06.250 --> 01:31:08.950
I'll write you, too.

01:31:13.120 --> 01:31:16.660
I put the diary and painting
back where I found them.

01:31:16.750 --> 01:31:18.790
Good, it's for the best.

01:31:19.450 --> 01:31:21.290
I haven't told my family.

01:31:22.080 --> 01:31:23.950
Let's keep it our secret.

01:31:26.950 --> 01:31:28.290
How funny...

01:31:30.120 --> 01:31:32.910
Marnie brought us together.

01:31:33.790 --> 01:31:34.790
That's true.

01:31:36.750 --> 01:31:37.790
Marnie...

01:31:41.410 --> 01:31:45.620
The girl trapped behind the blue window...

01:31:47.120 --> 01:31:49.000
That was long ago.

01:31:53.540 --> 01:31:57.580
<i>Exactly, he does it to save her life.</i>

01:31:57.660 --> 01:31:59.080
<i>I love that part.</i>

01:31:59.160 --> 01:32:02.160
<i>Ah, now I want to read it all over again.</i>

01:32:03.000 --> 01:32:04.750
I'll lend you the sequel.

01:32:04.830 --> 01:32:06.160
Anna!

01:32:10.160 --> 01:32:11.330
Auntie!

01:32:14.160 --> 01:32:15.500
Anna...

01:32:17.660 --> 01:32:19.750
Hey, be careful!

01:32:19.830 --> 01:32:21.160
Sorry, sorry.

01:32:28.290 --> 01:32:30.000
Auntie's here.

01:32:30.870 --> 01:32:33.700
Ah, Yoriko, you're here.

01:32:36.370 --> 01:32:38.290
Thank you for everything.

01:32:38.370 --> 01:32:41.700
She's doing well, and even made a friend.

01:32:42.370 --> 01:32:44.080
How can I ever repay you?

01:32:44.160 --> 01:32:48.040
Oh, no. We didn't do anything at all.

01:32:48.370 --> 01:32:50.200
Anna is a good girl.

01:32:50.290 --> 01:32:53.540
It was like having our own daughter back.

01:32:54.330 --> 01:32:55.540
She's welcome anytime.

01:32:56.250 --> 01:32:57.540
Thank you.

01:32:57.620 --> 01:32:58.870
Let's talk inside.

01:33:01.700 --> 01:33:05.200
I'm impressed.
You didn't call us once!

01:33:18.750 --> 01:33:20.410
I'm all packed.

01:33:21.250 --> 01:33:22.250
Anna.

01:33:23.870 --> 01:33:24.750
Yes?

01:33:26.080 --> 01:33:29.370
There's something I need to tell you.

01:33:31.450 --> 01:33:36.080
We receive monthly subsidies
to cover your expenses.

01:33:36.580 --> 01:33:37.870
We receive money.

01:33:38.580 --> 01:33:41.750
I've long hesitated to tell you, but--

01:33:41.830 --> 01:33:44.000
-It's okay.
-But believe me...

01:33:44.410 --> 01:33:46.910
Whether or not we receive money,

01:33:47.250 --> 01:33:49.120
it doesn't change our love for you.

01:33:50.750 --> 01:33:52.080
I already knew.

01:33:52.580 --> 01:33:55.200
I'm happy you told me about it.

01:33:55.290 --> 01:33:56.290
Anna!

01:34:01.120 --> 01:34:04.370
I've been looking at the photos you sent.

01:34:05.620 --> 01:34:06.620
Photos?

01:34:06.950 --> 01:34:11.700
Oh, while you were away
I was looking at old albums

01:34:11.790 --> 01:34:13.370
and found this picture.

01:34:13.790 --> 01:34:14.950
Do you remember?

01:34:17.950 --> 01:34:19.370
It's that mansion.

01:34:19.450 --> 01:34:23.000
When you first came to us,
you wouldn't let it go.

01:34:25.620 --> 01:34:27.500
I was told at the orphanage

01:34:28.370 --> 01:34:30.620
it belonged to your grandmother.

01:34:34.950 --> 01:34:38.120
MY BELOVED HOME - MARNIE

01:34:39.290 --> 01:34:40.500
Marnie!

01:35:19.370 --> 01:35:21.540
So that's who she was.

01:35:24.040 --> 01:35:25.040
Anna.

01:35:28.540 --> 01:35:32.870
<i>And so I was in the silo all night.</i>

01:35:33.200 --> 01:35:35.700
I was very frightened.

01:35:36.410 --> 01:35:38.870
That's when your grandpa came.

01:35:39.700 --> 01:35:42.870
He encouraged me, saying I did well.

01:35:43.540 --> 01:35:47.120
I've overcome many frightening things.

01:35:47.200 --> 01:35:48.870
And so will you, Anna.

01:35:50.200 --> 01:35:51.200
After all,

01:35:51.540 --> 01:35:56.200
you're my one and only grandchild.

01:35:58.910 --> 01:36:00.250
Grandma...

01:36:45.120 --> 01:36:46.250
Excuse me.

01:36:48.290 --> 01:36:49.290
Anna.

01:36:50.790 --> 01:36:52.790
I'm sorry for what I said.

01:36:55.120 --> 01:36:57.450
Next year, you better join us
to pick up the trash.

01:37:05.120 --> 01:37:05.950
A friend?

01:37:06.290 --> 01:37:07.290
Maybe.

01:37:14.000 --> 01:37:15.500
Hisako!

01:37:19.160 --> 01:37:20.330
Anna.

01:37:20.830 --> 01:37:23.450
I'm going home to Sapporo now.

01:37:23.540 --> 01:37:24.870
Is that right?

01:37:25.620 --> 01:37:29.120
But your face tells me
something good happened.

01:37:29.700 --> 01:37:32.750
Yes, I'm really happy now.

01:37:32.830 --> 01:37:33.870
Good.

01:37:34.870 --> 01:37:37.200
Um, this is my mother.

01:37:38.410 --> 01:37:41.620
Thank you for being kind to Anna.

01:37:42.250 --> 01:37:44.200
Oh no, it was my pleasure.

01:37:44.830 --> 01:37:47.120
Let's draw together again.

01:37:47.200 --> 01:37:48.120
Yes.

01:37:48.200 --> 01:37:51.450
I'll write you.
I have some amazing news.

01:37:51.540 --> 01:37:52.620
Goodbye.

01:37:54.700 --> 01:37:56.870
Thank you very much.

01:38:02.290 --> 01:38:03.830
Amazing news?

01:38:03.910 --> 01:38:06.000
Yeah, I'll tell you later.

01:38:06.410 --> 01:38:08.000
Oh, why not now?

01:38:08.080 --> 01:38:09.910
I promise I'll tell you.

01:38:20.950 --> 01:38:25.080
Toichi! Sayaka! Goodbye!

01:42:26.080 --> 01:42:31.200
THE END

01:42:35.000 --> 01:42:37.000
Subtitle translation by Taro Goto
